# Shell scripts MUST stay LF, even on Windows (core.autocrlf=true).
# A CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/bash\r`) makes a git hook fail with "bad interpreter",
# which would BLOCK commits instead of failing open -- see scripts/precommit-build-guard.sh
# and scripts/install-hooks.sh. Pinning eol=lf prevents that on fresh clones.
*.sh text eol=lf
